title: The wire — scene lifecycle and advertised responses
story: ides-of-march
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: Opening the poet's plain question puts its lifecycle on the
  scene channel and its advertised responses — answers and the
  inalienable silence — on the exchange-affordances channel; manner
  coloring rides the utterances; answering closes the exchange and the
  advertisement clears.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/ides-of-march/chord/ides-of-march.story
    stories/ides-of-march/tests/transcripts/wire.transcript
channels: scene, exchange-affordances

---

> north
[OK: contains "Stage"]

> west
[OK: contains "Tiring-House"]

# First contact opens the scene on the wire.
> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "The new hired man"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "scene-opened"]

# The book row opens the plain question: lifecycle on the scene
# channel, advertised responses on exchange-affordances — the authored
# answers and the silence that is always available.
> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "So it is not carried"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "character.exchange.opened"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "the-plain-question"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, contains "the-plain-question"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, contains "a spy"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, contains "henslowe"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, contains "silence"]

# The gripped answer serves with manner coloring on the utterance,
# and the advertisement clears with the close — never stale choices.
> ask shakespeare about a hired man
[OK: contains "the most crowded parish in England"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "utterance"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, not contains "the-plain-question"]
